DATASETS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. SMS Phishing Dataset for Machine Learning and Pattern Recognition (Mendeley Data, V1)
   Authors: Sandhya Mishra, Devpriya Soni (2022). DOI: 10.17632/f45bkkt8pr.1
   Source:  https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f45bkkt8pr/1
   Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Use:     Training and held-out testing of the text model (smishing = scam, ham = genuine; spam used only to measure
            how often marketing is flagged). Not redistributed.

2. SMS Spam Collection (UCI Machine Learning Repository, dataset 228)
   Authors: Tiago A. Almeida, José María Gómez Hidalgo (2011). DOI: 10.24432/C5CC84
   Source:  https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/228/sms+spam+collection
   Licence: CC BY 4.0 - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Use:     Not downloaded directly. Credited because most of dataset 1's genuine ("ham") messages come from this collection.

3. BothBosu scam dialogue datasets: scam-dialogue, single-agent-scam-conversations, multi-agent-scam-conversation
   Authors: BothBosu (Pitipat Gumphusiri, Tuul Triyason), "Synthetic Data for Scam Detection: Leveraging LLMs to Train
            Deep Learning Models", IEEE/WIC WI-IAT 2024.
   Source:  https://huggingface.co/datasets/BothBosu/scam-dialogue
            https://huggingface.co/datasets/BothBosu/single-agent-scam-conversations
            https://huggingface.co/datasets/BothBosu/multi-agent-scam-conversation
   Licence: Apache License 2.0 - https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
   Use:     Training (weight 0.5, scam vs genuine only) and held-out testing. Not redistributed.

4. Fishing for Smishing: SMS phishing reports dataset (ACM IMC 2025 artifact)
   Authors: Sharad Agarwal, Antonis Papasavva, Guillermo Suarez-Tangil, Marie Vasek. "Fishing for Smishing: Understanding
            SMS Phishing Infrastructure and Strategies by Mining Public User Reports", Proceedings of the 2025 ACM Internet
            Measurement Conference (IMC '25). DOI: 10.1145/3730567.3764431
   Source:  https://github.com/reportsmishing/Smishing-Dataset-IMC25
   Licence: CC BY 4.0 - https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Use:     Evaluation (held-out recall on real smishing). A training slice was tried only in a rejected experiment.
            Not redistributed.

5. Indian Scam SMS (synthetic, audited)
