8. ICFD-31k: Indian Conversational Fraud Dataset. EVALUATION ONLY, NOT REDISTRIBUTED.
   Citation: Rishi Ahuja, Kumar Prateek, Simranjit Singh. "ICFD-31k: A Large-Scale Dataset and Benchmark for Real-Time
            Conversational Fraud Detection." In Proceedings of the Thirty-Fifth International Joint Conference on
            Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI-ECAI), 2026.
   Source:  https://huggingface.co/datasets/rishia2220/icfd-31k   (code: https://github.com/SPELLAILab/ICFD-31k)
   Licence: ICFD-31k Data Use Terms (defensive research, education and benchmarking; no commercial deployment without the
            authors' written permission) - https://github.com/SPELLAILab/ICFD-31k/blob/main/LICENSE-DATA.md
   Use:     Benchmarking only: Ruko measures recall on the test and cross-domain splits. The shipped model is NOT trained on
            ICFD-31k, and no ICFD-31k content is stored in this repository.

Ruko's own data (MIT, this repository):
   - ml/data/synthetic/ruko_synth_v1.jsonl: synthetic dialogues and messages generated with LLMs on Nebius Token Factory
     (Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507; google/gemma-3-27b-it for the held-out generator). Every row is labelled synthetic.
   - ml/data/realworld/realworld_eval.jsonl: our own paraphrases of real cases and messages. Each row cites its source URL.
     The text is ours (MIT); the facts come from the cited sources.
   - data/patterns/: the scam pattern library. Its text paraphrases the sources listed in data/patterns/sources.json,
     with short quotes only.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TEXT MODEL
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

server/ml/model/ruko-text-v1.json (ruko-text-1.0.0) was trained on Ruko's synthetic set (MIT), the BothBosu datasets
(Apache-2.0, item 3) and the Mendeley SMS Phishing Dataset (CC BY 4.0, item 1, which includes UCI SMS Spam Collection
messages, item 2). It was evaluated, but not trained, on items 4-8. See ml/MODEL_CARD.md.

